  "aiContextParagraph": "Eight-time world champion Marc Marquez has officially announced his retirement from MotoGP at the end of the 2026 season. The decision follows a series of physical challenges, with the rider identifying significant accidents at the Mandalika and Le Mans circuits as primary contributors to his choice. Ahead of his final event at the Ricardo Tormo circuit, Marquez notably set a new lap record during practice sessions for the Valencia Grand Prix. The announcement arrived unexpectedly for his team, Ducati, with representatives Gigi Dall'Igna and Davide Tardozzi stating they were unaware of the decision until shortly before it was made public. Despite the retirement plans, the rider remains under contract with Ducati through 2028, leading the team to begin evaluating potential successors for the upcoming seasons. Fellow riders and team staff have acknowledged the news as a significant moment for the paddock.",
